GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_infer_owl_dl.py> {
    ns111:test_infer_owl_dl.py dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_infer_owl_dl" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """tests/unit/test_infer_owl_dl.py

Coverage for StarLayerGraph.infer(entailment=ENTAILMENT['OWL-Direct'], engine="hermit") -
OWL 2 Direct Semantics reasoning via owlready2 + Java HermiT, a genuinely
different computational model (tableau DL reasoning) from every owlrl-backed
entailment regime covered by test_infer.py. `owlready2` is an optional extra of this
package (`pip install starlayer.graph[hermit]`), not a core dependency -
the `owl_dl_extra` skip below is a real "not opted into this engine" skip,
the same spirit as test_infer_owl_dl_rustdl.py's own skip for `[rustdl]`.
A real Java runtime on PATH is a *further* prerequisite that genuinely
can't be satisfied by `pip` alone even once the extra is installed -
HermiT is a Java program, not a pure-Python one - so it gets its own,
separate skip condition.

Per this project's own testing discipline (starlayer.sparql/CLAUDE.md: "any new
query/update shape needs an execution-comparison test, not just a
structural one"), the key test here uses a disjunctive entailment
(`Person subClassOf (Man or Woman)`, `Man`/`Woman` disjoint, `not-Man`
asserted) that owlrl's forward-chaining rule engine structurally cannot
derive - proving this entailment regime is doing genuine DL reasoning, not
something already covered by entailment=ENTAILMENT['OWL-RDF-Based'].""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_infer_owl_dl" ;
        slkg:declares ns244:test_engine_rejected_for_non_owl_dl_entailment, ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment, ns244:TestOwlDlSubClassClosure, ns244:test_invalid_engine_raises_value_error, ns244:test_missing_java_raises_a_distinct_clear_error, ns244:TestOwlDlTimeout, ns244:TestOwlDlModes, ns244:test_missing_owlready2_raises_actionable_error, ns244:TestOwlDlInconsistency, ns244:test_broken_java_raises_a_distinct_clear_error, ns244:test_timeout_rejected_for_non_owl_dl_entailment ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_infer_owl_dl.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:owlready2, ns4:pytest, ns4:shutil, ns4:os .

    ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_infer_owl_dl.TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """The oracle-comparison case: owlrl's forward-chaining rule engine
structurally cannot derive a disjunctive entailment (it would need to
case-split on `owl:unionOf`, which no Horn rule can express) - so a
correct result here proves entailment=ENTAILMENT['OWL-Direct'] is genuine DL reasoning,
not something entailment=ENTAILMENT['OWL-RDF-Based'] could already produce.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment" ;
        slkg:declares ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment.test_owlrl_cannot_derive_this, ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment.test_original_graph_untouched_by_mode_full, ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment.test_owl_dl_derives_the_disjunctive_entailment, ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment.test_delta_contains_just_the_new_fact, ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment._disjunctive_graph ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_infer_owl_dl.py" ;
        slkg:hasDecorator ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment.decorator.1, ns244:TestOwlDlDisjunctiveEntailment.decorator.0 ;
        slkg:lineEnd 100 ;
        slkg:lineStart 55 .

