    ns300:TestBoundBlankNodeLookups.test_list_nodes_sharing_a_first_value_stay_distinct dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.integration.test_oxigraph_store_rdf12.TestBoundBlankNodeLookups.test_list_nodes_sharing_a_first_value_stay_distinct" ;
        a slkg:Method ;
        rdfs:comment """Two RDF lists with a node that has the same rdf:first ("big").

The native read path used to re-identify a bound blank node by a
content join on one of its own triples ("the node whose rdf:first is
'big'"), which matched BOTH nodes and returned the other list's
rdf:rest too - so Graph.items() sometimes dropped an element,
depending on result-row order. Found by running the W3C SHACL
node-expression fixtures through the store. Repeated over fresh
graphs because the failure depended on engine row order.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_list_nodes_sharing_a_first_value_stay_distinct" ;
        slkg:calls ns300:_oxigraph_graph ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/integration/test_oxigraph_store_rdf12.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 471 ;
        slkg:lineStart 452 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_list_nodes_sharing_a_first_value_stay_distinct(self)" .

