    ns75:StarShaclSchema dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.validator.StarShaclSchema" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """A SHACL schema: a bound shapes graph plus an optional ontology
graph, to validate, infer rules against, or evaluate node
expressions over any number of data graphs.

``self.shacl_graph``/``self.ont_graph`` are each a reference to
their own separate graph - this class does not itself *hold* triples
the way ``StarLayerGraph`` does. Composition, not inheritance: there
is no real "is-a" relationship available between it and any
existing rdflib/pyshacl class - pySHACL's own main entry point,
``validate()``, is a stateless one-shot function, not a long-lived
object to subclass, and this class unifies several independent
capabilities (``validate``/``apply_rules``/``evaluate``) rather than
specializing any one of them. Construct one per distinct shapes-set
(``PersonSchema = StarShaclSchema(person_shapes)``,
``ProductSchema = StarShaclSchema(product_shapes)``, ...), then call
``validate``/``apply_rules``/``evaluate`` against whatever data graph
you're checking. ``select_widgets`` is the one method that needs no data
graph at all - it chooses SHACL 1.2 UI widgets from the shapes graph alone. Shape-driven subgraph extraction is a separate, plain
function (``starlayer.shacl.extract_subgraph()``), not a method here -
see its own docstring, and the subgraph-extraction guide, for why.

Adds RDF 1.2/triple-term adaptation around pySHACL, which understands
neither triple terms nor SHACL 1.2's own predicates natively.""" ;
        rdfs:label "StarShaclSchema" ;
        slkg:declares ns75:StarShaclSchema.build_report, ns75:StarShaclSchema.evaluate, ns75:StarShaclSchema.select_widgets, ns75:StarShaclSchema.extract_shapes_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema._annotate_used_graphs_and_configuration, ns75:StarShaclSchema._strip_deactivated_node_expressions, ns75:StarShaclSchema._augment_shapes_with_new_target_types, ns75:StarShaclSchema.evaluate_component, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_literal_only_component_name, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_shacl_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema._try_native_core_validation, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_shapes_graph_and_provenance, ns75:StarShaclSchema._annotate_conformance_disallows, ns75:StarShaclSchema._try_native_structural_property_validation, ns75:StarShaclSchema._try_native_literal_only_validation, ns75:StarShaclSchema._humanize_report_text, ns75:StarShaclSchema.validate, ns75:StarShaclSchema.__init__, ns75:StarShaclSchema._nodes_conforming_to, ns75:StarShaclSchema.validate_each, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_structural_component_definition, ns75:StarShaclSchema.apply_rules, ns75:StarShaclSchema._resolve_data_graph, ns75:StarShaclSchema._ensure_native_component_shapes_typed, ns75:StarShaclSchema.close_shape, ns75:StarShaclSchema.target_nodes ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/validator.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 2154 ;
        slkg:lineStart 81 .

