GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/test_mc_generated.py> {
    ns334:test_mc_generated.py dcterms:identifier "tests.starontology.manchester_conformance.test_mc_generated" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Grammar-driven property tests (Hypothesis): random valid Manchester documents, tree invariants checked.

Hand-written cases find the gaps someone thought to probe; a generator finds the combinations nobody did
(a restriction inside a negation inside a union inside a ``that`` list...). Documents are built from the
W3C productions the parser *supports today*; constructs recorded as findings in ``known_failures.py``
are deliberately excluded here and enter the generator as their gaps are closed.

Invariants per generated document: the parse succeeds; the tree validates; ``tree -> OWL`` is isomorphic
to compiling the text directly; the rendered text re-parses to the same OWL; a second tree pass is stable.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_mc_generated" ;
        slkg:declares ns341:axiom_text, ns341:test_generated_documents_hold_the_tree_invariants, ns341:annotation_prefix, ns341:class_expr, ns341:data_range ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/starontology/manchester_conformance/test_mc_generated.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:hypothesis, ns4:pytest, ns4:os, ns4:__future__ .

