    ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_conformance.TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """RDF/XML's version mechanism is structurally different from every
other format's - an rdf:version XML attribute on a node/property
element (confirmed via spec fetch), not a prologue-line directive.

Found via a live Oxigraph 0.5.9 round trip (2026-07-17): it genuinely
emits rdf:version on the property element wrapping rdf:parseType="Triple"
for a reified triple term. Feeding that real output into starlayer.graph's own
parser revealed this wasn't just "unimplemented" - it was actively wrong:
rdflib's real 'xml' parser treats any attribute it doesn't specifically
recognize as ordinary RDF/XML "property attribute" shorthand, so an
unstripped rdf:version asserted a bogus extra triple
(subject, rdf:version, "1.2") into the graph.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute" ;
        slkg:declares ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_no_version_attribute_does_not_warn, ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_version_1_2_full_does_not_warn, ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_real_oxigraph_output_does_not_produce_bogus_triple, ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_1_2_basic_with_triple_term_warns, ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_real_oxigraph_output_extracts_declared_version ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_conformance.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 553 ;
        slkg:lineStart 493 .

    ns189:TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_1_2_basic_with_triple_term_warns dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_conformance.TestRdfXmlVersionAttribute.test_1_2_basic_with_triple_term_warns" ;
