GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/model/conformance.py> {
    ns1:conformance.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.model.conformance" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starlayer.graph.model.conformance

RDF 1.2 / SPARQL 1.2 VERSION-directive conformance checking.

Per RDF 1.2 Concepts sec 2.1 ("Version Labels") and SPARQL 1.2 Query sec 4.3,
three version labels are defined:

    "1.2"        full RDF 1.2 conformance - triple terms and dirLangString allowed
    "1.2-basic"  RDF 1.2 syntax, but excludes triple terms and dirLangString
    "1.1"        legacy RDF 1.1 compatibility mode (discouraged in a VERSION
                 directive, since it would needlessly break RDF 1.1 parsers)

The directive is explicitly only a hint: the spec states a parser "is not
required to reject features that are outside the announced version (but
could signal them with a warning)", and the SPARQL spec similarly says
"processors may treat unrecognized labels as an error or as a warning" -
neither mandates specific behavior. StarLayer signals via a warning, never a
hard error, to stay consistent with its permissive-by-default posture: a
stale-but-harmless VERSION line should never turn otherwise-valid data or a
otherwise-valid query into a hard failure.

Two distinct warning classes are used, per SPARQL 1.2 Query sec 4.3's own
observation that "the SPARQL version labels refer to SPARQL syntax and
semantics, while the RDF version labels refer to RDF syntax and semantics":
RDF12ConformanceWarning for RDF document formats (Turtle, TriG,
N-Triples/N-Quads, RDF/XML), SPARQL12ConformanceWarning for a SPARQL
query/update's own VERSION directive.""" ;
        rdfs:label "conformance" ;
        slkg:declares ns3:RDF12ConformanceWarning, ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs, ns3:SPARQL12ConformanceWarning, ns3:check_version_conformance ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/model/conformance.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:warnings .

    ns3:RDF12ConformanceWarning dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.model.conformance.RDF12ConformanceWarning" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """A declared VERSION label doesn't match the RDF 1.2 features actually
used in an RDF document (Turtle, TriG, N-Triples/N-Quads, RDF/XML).""" ;
        rdfs:label "RDF12ConformanceWarning" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns4:builtins.UserWarning ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/model/conformance.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 38 ;
        slkg:lineStart 36 .

    ns3:SPARQL12ConformanceWarning dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.model.conformance.SPARQL12ConformanceWarning" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """A declared VERSION label doesn't match the RDF 1.2 features actually
used in a SPARQL query/update's own text.

Deliberately not a subclass of RDF12ConformanceWarning: per SPARQL 1.2
Query sec 4.3, "the SPARQL version labels refer to SPARQL syntax and
semantics, while the RDF version labels refer to RDF syntax and
semantics" - the two directives share label spelling but check a
different kind of conformance, so they get distinct warning classes.""" ;
        rdfs:label "SPARQL12ConformanceWarning" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns4:builtins.UserWarning ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/model/conformance.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 50 ;
        slkg:lineStart 41 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.model.conformance.check_version_conformance" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Warn if declared_version is unrecognized, or is "1.2-basic"/"1.1" while
a triple term and/or dirLangString is actually present.

"1.1" is included alongside "1.2-basic" here, not just "1.2-basic": "1.1"
means plain RDF 1.1 syntax/semantics, which by definition has neither of
the two RDF 1.2 additions this project tracks (see the README's own
scope note) - so it excludes triple terms/dirLangString at least as
strictly as "1.2-basic" does, not more permissively.

declared_version -- the VERSION directive's label, or None if no
                     directive was present (in which case this is a no-op)
context           -- short label identifying what was checked, for the
                      warning message, e.g. "Turtle document" or
                      "SPARQL query"
warning_class     -- RDF12ConformanceWarning (default) for RDF document
                      formats, or SPARQL12ConformanceWarning for a
                      SPARQL query/update's own VERSION directive
stacklevel        -- passed straight to warnings.warn(); the default (3)
                      is correct for a direct caller (warn's own frame,
                      then this function's, then the caller's - pointing
                      the warning at the caller's line). A wrapper that
                      itself calls this function - e.g.
                      check_version_conformance_for_graphs() below -
                      should pass stacklevel=4 so the warning still
                      points at *its* caller, not at the wrapper itself.""" ;
        rdfs:label "check_version_conformance" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/model/conformance.py" ;
        slkg:hasParameter ns3:check_version_conformance.param.stacklevel, ns3:check_version_conformance.param.uses_triple_term, ns3:check_version_conformance.param.declared_version, ns3:check_version_conformance.param.warning_class, ns3:check_version_conformance.param.context, ns3:check_version_conformance.param.uses_dirlangstring ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns3:check_version_conformance.returns ;
        slkg:lineEnd 109 ;
        slkg:lineStart 53 ;
        slkg:signature "def check_version_conformance(declared_version, *, uses_triple_term: bool, uses_dirlangstring: bool, context: str, warning_class: type=RDF12ConformanceWarning, stacklevel: int=3) -> None" .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.param.context a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "context" ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 3 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.param.declared_version a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "declared_version" ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 0 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.param.stacklevel a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "stacklevel" ;
        slkg:annotationText "int" ;
        slkg:defaultValue "3" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.int ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 5 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.param.uses_dirlangstring a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "uses_dirlangstring" ;
        slkg:annotationText "bool" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.bool ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 2 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.param.uses_triple_term a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "uses_triple_term" ;
        slkg:annotationText "bool" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.bool ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 1 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.param.warning_class a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "warning_class" ;
        slkg:annotationText "type" ;
        slkg:defaultValue "RDF12ConformanceWarning" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.type ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 4 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.model.conformance.check_version_conformance_for_graphs" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Convenience wrapper: computes uses_triple_term/uses_dirlangstring by
scanning the given StarLayerGraph(s) (their _tt_nodes registry and
triples() for a DirLangString object), then calls
check_version_conformance().

Shared by StarLayerGraph.parse()'s per-format branches (Turtle,
N-Triples/N-Quads, TriG, RDF/XML each pass graphs=[self]) and
StarLayerDataset (passes graphs=self.contexts(), since a document-level
VERSION directive covers every named graph, not just one) - previously
each of those call sites duplicated this exact scan inline.""" ;
        rdfs:label "check_version_conformance_for_graphs" ;
        slkg:calls ns3:check_version_conformance ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/model/conformance.py" ;
        slkg:hasParameter ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.param.context, ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.param.declared_version, ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.param.graphs ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.returns ;
        slkg:lineEnd 138 ;
        slkg:lineStart 112 ;
        slkg:signature "def check_version_conformance_for_graphs(declared_version, graphs, *, context: str) -> None" .

    ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.param.context a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "context" ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 2 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.param.declared_version a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "declared_version" ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 0 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.param.graphs a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "graphs" ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 1 .

    ns3:check_version_conformance_for_graphs.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns4:builtins.UserWarning dcterms:identifier "builtins.UserWarning" ;
        a slkg:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "UserWarning" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf slkg:Type .

    ns4:builtins.bool dcterms:identifier "builtins.bool" ;
        a slkg:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "bool" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf slkg:Type .

    ns4:builtins.int dcterms:identifier "builtins.int" ;
        a slkg:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "int" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf slkg:Type .

    ns4:builtins.str dcterms:identifier "builtins.str" ;
        a slkg:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "str" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf slkg:Type .

    ns4:builtins.type dcterms:identifier "builtins.type" ;
        a slkg:ExternalType ;
