GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/sqe_coverage/test_sqe_property_based.py> {
    ns319:test_sqe_property_based.py dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_sqe_property_based" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Property-based probing of sqe with Hypothesis.

Random but valid SPARQL queries are generated over the synthetic dataset's
vocabulary (the generator tracks which variables are bound, so every query is
well formed), and each is held to these properties:

1. it parses to an sqe tree that passes the sqe shapes and holds no salg: terms;
2. the text rendered from the tree is stable: parsing it again and rendering
   again gives the same text;
3. the regenerated text returns the same rows as the original query on a
   StarLayerDataset (this is the property that catches a silently dropped clause);
4. the decoded ``Query`` object also decodes without error.

Opt-in (``pytest --sqe-coverage``). The number of examples per property comes
from ``STARLAYER_SQE_FUZZ_EXAMPLES`` (default 60); Hypothesis shrinks any
failure to the smallest query that still fails and prints it.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_sqe_property_based" ;
        slkg:declares ns331:test_tree_is_valid_text_is_stable_and_rows_match, ns331:_ask_query, ns331:_group, ns331:_triple, ns331:_boolean, ns331:_string, ns331:test_decoded_query_object_returns_the_same_rows, ns331:_select_query, ns331:_canonical_rows, ns331:_construct_query, ns331:_numeric ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/sqe_coverage/test_sqe_property_based.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_w3c_through_sqe, ns4:tests.sparql.sqe_coverage.test_sqe_features, ns4:pytest, ns4:os, ns4:__future__, ns4:hypothesis .

