GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/codekg/extractor/stamp.py> {
    ns276:stamp.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.codekg.extractor.stamp" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starlayer.codekg.extractor.stamp - the build stamp, and the freshness of the graph against the source.

``write_stamp()`` records one ``slkg:KGBuild`` node (time, git commit, whether the working tree had uncommitted Python
changes, file count) in its own named graph of ``codekg.trig``. ``freshness()`` compares a stamp with the repository
as it is now. ``append_changelog_entry()`` adds an automatic line to ``codekg/CHANGELOG.md``.

All the git calls are best effort: no git, no repository or a shallow clone just leaves the commit out.""" ;
        rdfs:label "stamp" ;
        slkg:declares ns353:_git, ns353:append_changelog_entry, ns353:freshness, ns353:write_stamp, ns353:head_commit, ns353:Freshness, ns353:uncommitted_python_changes ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/codekg/extractor/stamp.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:__future__, ns4:dataclasses, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:pathlib, ns4:subprocess, ns4:rdflib, ns4:datetime, ns4:re .

