GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/w3c_shacl12/known_failures.py> {
    ns100:known_failures.py dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.w3c_shacl12.known_failures" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Registry of W3C SHACL 1.2 suite entries with a known, reasoned disposition.

Per CLAUDE.md's testing-coverage discipline, a failing conformance test is
never silently skipped - every entry here names *why* (a specific
docs/shacl12-gap-matrix.md "Not Covered / Deferred" row, a specific
docs/upstream-issues/pyshacl-upstream-issues.md entry, or a concrete Working-Draft-churn
explanation) and is applied as ``pytest.xfail(strict=True)``, so it breaks
loudly (as an unexpected XPASS) the moment the underlying gap is closed
instead of silently going stale.

Review this file the same way the gap matrix's own tables are reviewed:
every entry is a claim that should still be true, not a historical record.

Keyed by ids.portable_id(entry, VENDOR_ROOT) - a path-relative id, *not*
str(entry.iri) (which is an absolute file:// path that differs across
machines/checkouts, unsuitable for a committed file). This is also the
pytest parametrize id, so a failing test's node id can be pasted directly
in as a key here.""" ;
        rdfs:label "known_failures" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/w3c_shacl12/known_failures.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:__future__ .

    ns4:__future__ a slkg:ExternalModule .
}

GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_infer.py> {
    ns111:test_infer.py dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_infer" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """tests/unit/test_infer.py

Coverage for StarLayerGraph.infer(), which formalizes the manual
owlrl.DeductiveClosure workflow shown in docs/guides/02b-graphs-inferencing.ipynb
into real API. Per this project's own testing discipline (starlayer.sparql/CLAUDE.md:
"any new query/update shape needs an execution-comparison test, not just a
structural one"), every test here compares infer()'s output against owlrl
itself run directly - owlrl is the oracle, since plain rdflib has no
entailment of its own to compare against.

Requires the `reasoning` extra: pip install -e ".[reasoning]\"""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_infer" ;
        slkg:declares ns197:TestInferCombinedRegime, ns197:_rdfs_graph, ns197:TestInferCombinedWithRdf, ns197:TestInferOwlRl, ns197:TestInferDelta, ns197:TestInferRdf, ns197:TestInferRdfs, ns197:TestInferInPlace, ns197:TestInferWithTripleTerms ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_infer.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:rdflib, ns4:pytest, ns4:owlrl, ns4:rdflib.namespace .

