GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/w3c_sparql12/download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py> {
    ns107:download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.w3c_sparql12.download_w3c_sparql12_tests" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """W3C SPARQL 1.2 Test Suite download script.

Downloads manifest.ttl and every file it references (queries, data, expected
results) for a fixed set of manifest categories from a single pinned-commit
tarball snapshot of the official test suite at
https://github.com/w3c/rdf-tests/tree/main/sparql/sparql12 - a real,
separate test suite from starlayer.graph's own tests/w3c_turtle12/
(Turtle-1.2-only, a different repo path). Mirrors
scripts/sync_w3c_shacl12_suite.py's own fetch shape (one tarball request,
pinned SHA, deliberate bump, a VENDORED_FROM.md provenance stamp) rather than
this script's own prior per-file ``requests.get()`` design, which risked
GitHub's 60-req/hour unauthenticated rate limit and left no record of what
was actually fetched.

The manifest itself is still parsed as real Turtle via rdflib, not regex -
the SPARQL 1.2 manifests nest mf:action as a blank node with qt:query/qt:data
(or ut:request for updates), which a line-oriented regex scan can't recover
reliably.

Categories fetched (see this suite's own index at
https://w3c.github.io/rdf-tests/sparql/sparql12/ for the full list of 10):
  - syntax-triple-terms-positive / -negative: PositiveSyntaxTest/
    NegativeSyntaxTest(/Update variants) - parse-only checks.
  - eval-triple-terms: QueryEvaluationTest/UpdateEvaluationTest - full
    execution checks (Update ones are fetched for completeness but this
    project can't run them yet - no Update serialization, see CLAUDE.md).
  - expression: QueryEvaluationTest for isTRIPLE/SUBJECT/PREDICATE/OBJECT.
  - lang-basedir/codepoint-escapes/grouping/rdf11/syntax/version - added
    2026-10-13 (previously the only unfetched six; see
    starlayer/graph/CLAUDE.md's dated entry for why lang-basedir in
    particular was worth adding - several real starlayer.sparql gaps were
    found and fixed through it). Several fixtures across these are
    believed, confirmed-against-plain-rdflib defects inherited from
    rdflib itself, not this project's own gap - see
    tests/sparql/w3c_sparql12/test_w3c_sparql12.py's own
    _KNOWN_SUITE_DEFECT_FRAGMENTS/_INHERITED_RDFLIB_GAP_FRAGMENTS for the
    full, individually-reasoned list.

Bumping PINNED_SHA is a deliberate, one-line, reviewable change - this
script never auto-follows ``main``'s tip. The companion Turtle 1.2 downloader
(tests/graph/w3c_turtle12/) and this script's own sibling copy
(tests/graph/w3c_sparql12/) pull from the same w3c/rdf-tests repo at their
own independently-pinned SHA; bump all affected scripts together when
investigating a specific upstream change, but there's no requirement they
share one SHA otherwise.

Always re-fetches and overwrites (the source is a pinned, immutable commit,
so there's nothing to gain from skipping files already on disk - unlike a
live, unpinned fetch, re-running this can never produce different output
until PINNED_SHA is bumped).

Usage: python download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py""" ;
        rdfs:label "download_w3c_sparql12_tests" ;
        slkg:declares ns162:_local_filename, ns162:fetch_category, ns162:main, ns162:_fetch_tarball_members ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/w3c_sparql12/download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:os, ns4:__future__, ns4:tarfile, ns4:io, ns4:urllib.request, ns4:datetime, ns4:rdflib, ns4:rdflib.namespace .

    ns162:_fetch_tarball_members dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.w3c_sparql12.download_w3c_sparql12_tests._fetch_tarball_members" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment "{category: {relative_filename: bytes}} for each name in CATEGORIES." ;
        rdfs:label "_fetch_tarball_members" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/w3c_sparql12/download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py" ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns162:_fetch_tarball_members.returns ;
        slkg:isPrivate true ;
        slkg:lineEnd 124 ;
        slkg:lineStart 102 ;
        slkg:signature "def _fetch_tarball_members() -> dict[str, dict[str, bytes]]" .

    ns162:_fetch_tarball_members.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "dict[str, dict[str, bytes]]" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.dict, ns4:builtins.bytes, ns4:builtins.str .

    ns162:_local_filename dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.w3c_sparql12.download_w3c_sparql12_tests._local_filename" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """The manifest references files by IRI relative to the category's own
base URL - just the trailing path segment is the local filename.""" ;
        rdfs:label "_local_filename" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/w3c_sparql12/download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py" ;
        slkg:hasParameter ns162:_local_filename.param.iri ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns162:_local_filename.returns ;
        slkg:isPrivate true ;
        slkg:lineEnd 130 ;
        slkg:lineStart 127 ;
        slkg:signature "def _local_filename(iri: str) -> str" .

    ns162:_local_filename.param.iri a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "iri" ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 0 .

    ns162:_local_filename.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str .

    ns162:fetch_category dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.w3c_sparql12.download_w3c_sparql12_tests.fetch_category" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Write this category's manifest.ttl + every file it references from
the already-fetched tarball contents, return a list of test-entry dicts
for the combined index.""" ;
        rdfs:label "fetch_category" ;
        slkg:calls ns162:_local_filename ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/w3c_sparql12/download_w3c_sparql12_tests.py" ;
        slkg:hasParameter ns162:fetch_category.param.files, ns162:fetch_category.param.category ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns162:fetch_category.returns ;
        slkg:lineEnd 214 ;
        slkg:lineStart 133 ;
        slkg:signature "def fetch_category(category: str, files: dict[str, bytes]) -> list[dict]" .

    ns162:fetch_category.param.category a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "category" ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 0 .

    ns162:fetch_category.param.files a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "files" ;
        slkg:annotationText "dict[str, bytes]" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.bytes, ns4:builtins.str, ns4:builtins.dict ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 1 .

    ns162:fetch_category.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "list[dict]" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.list, ns4:builtins.dict .

    ns162:main dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.w3c_sparql12.download_w3c_sparql12_tests.main" ;
