    ns28:StarLayerGraph._native_add_many.param.skolemize_bnodes a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "``None`` (default) decides from the store: skolemize only on an engine whose blank-node ids are not stable across queries (``blank_node_ids_are_stable()``), where a real blank node could never be referred to again. Write blank nodes as their stable skolem URIs, exactly like ``add()`` does, instead of as real blank nodes. Real blank nodes get engine-assigned ids, so a ``BNode`` object that existed *before* the write (a label from some other graph, a variable the caller still holds) no longer names the stored node afterwards; skolemizing keeps the original label addressable, at the cost of the stored node not being a true blank node to ``isBLANK()``/``ORDER BY``. Use it when copying a graph whose existing ``BNode`` labels must keep working; leave it off for ``parse()``-style loads." ;
