    ns28:StarLayerGraph.serialize.param.format a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:comment "One of: - ``'turtle12'`` (default) — Turtle 1.2 with ``<<( )>>`` triple terms. - ``'longturtle12'`` — Turtle 1.2, one triple per line (no grouping). - ``'nt12'`` — N-Triples 1.2 with ``<<( )>>`` triple terms. - ``'nq12'`` — N-Quads 1.2 (graph name from ``self.identifier``). - ``'trig12'`` — TriG 1.2 (GRAPH block wrapper around Turtle 1.2). - ``'trix12'`` — TriX 1.2 XML (``<graph>`` block with ``<triple>`` elements). - ``'manchester'`` (alias ``'omn'``) — OWL 2 Manchester Syntax; see ``starlayer.graph.serializers.manchester``'s module docstring for the supported subset and known round-tripping limitations. - ``'n3'``/``'n3-12'``/``'text/n3'`` — aliased straight to ``'turtle12'``; only the plain-triples subset N3 shares with Turtle is supported, not real N3 (formulas, ``'=>'`` rules, ``'?x'`` variables) - see ``parse()``'s own note. - Any other format (e.g. ``'turtle'``, ``'xml'``) delegates to rdflib using the internal tt:HASH encoding - triple terms appear as opaque URIRefs." ;
        rdfs:label "format" ;
        slkg:defaultValue "'turtle12'" ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
