GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/rdfxml12.py> {
    ns11:rdfxml12.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.rdfxml12" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starlayer.graph.parsers.rdfxml12

Parse RDF/XML 1.2 text into (s, p, o) triples with TripleTerm objects.

rdflib's own 'xml' parser is RDF 1.1 only: it doesn't recognize
rdf:parseType="Triple" (falls back to treating it as XMLLiteral) or the
rdf:annotation/rdf:annotationNodeID reifier-shorthand attributes (mishandled
as ordinary, incorrectly-shaped properties - confirmed empirically, not
merely assumed). So this module preprocesses the raw XML tree with
ElementTree first: every rdf:parseType="Triple" property element and every
rdf:annotation/rdf:annotationNodeID attribute is rewritten into the same
bnode-based rdf:TripleTerm intermediate encoding StarLayerTurtleParser's
_skolemize_encoding() family already uses, which rdflib's real 'xml' parser
*does* understand correctly (they're just ordinary rdf:type/rdf:subject/
rdf:predicate/rdf:object triples at that point). The rest of the document -
everything that isn't one of those two RDF 1.2 additions - is left completely
untouched and parsed by rdflib exactly as before.

Scope: only node elements directly under <rdf:RDF> and their direct
property-element children are inspected for rdf:parseType="Triple" or
rdf:annotation/rdf:annotationNodeID (this matches exactly what
serialize_rdfxml12() emits). A property carrying rdf:annotation/
rdf:annotationNodeID must resolve to rdf:resource, an rdf:nodeID, a single
nested node element, or plain literal content; rdf:parseType="Resource"/
"Collection" combined with either attribute is out of scope and raises
NotImplementedError rather than being silently mishandled. A single
xml:base (if present on the document element) is honored for relative IRIs
in the parts this module resolves itself; per-element xml:base overrides are
not.

RDF 1.2's third addition, the rdf:version announcement attribute (RDF 1.2
XML Syntax: a version announcement on an in-scope node element with an
rdf:version attribute), is stripped wherever found on a node or property
element this module resolves, and recorded - not just unhandled but
actively dangerous to leave alone: rdflib's real 'xml' parser treats any
attribute it doesn't specifically recognize as RDF/XML's ordinary "property
attribute" shorthand, so an untouched rdf:version asserts a bogus extra
triple (subject rdf:version "value") into the graph - including on the
property element wrapping rdf:parseType="Triple", not just a node element.
See extract_version_directive() for the standalone scan used to surface the
value for StarLayerGraph.parse()'s RDF12ConformanceWarning check
(starlayer.graph.model.conformance).

Entry point:
    parse_rdfxml12(text) -> list of (s, p, o)""" ;
        rdfs:label "rdfxml12" ;
        slkg:declares ns17:extract_version_directive, ns17:_Preprocessor, ns17:_convert_bnodes, ns17:_local_to_uriref, ns17:parse_rdfxml12 ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/rdfxml12.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:xml.etree.ElementTree, ns4:urllib.parse, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:rdflib, ns4:__future__ .

    ns17:_Preprocessor dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.rdfxml12._Preprocessor" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """Rewrites rdf:parseType="Triple" and rdf:annotation/rdf:annotationNodeID
in place on an ElementTree, into the bnode-based rdf:TripleTerm
intermediate _convert_bnodes() (and rdflib's own 'xml' parser) understand.""" ;
        rdfs:label "_Preprocessor" ;
        slkg:declares ns17:_Preprocessor._fresh_id, ns17:_Preprocessor._strip_version_attr, ns17:_Preprocessor._resolve_object_from_property, ns17:_Preprocessor._emit_triple_term_block, ns17:_Preprocessor._process_property, ns17:_Preprocessor.__init__, ns17:_Preprocessor._resolve_node_element_subject, ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component, ns17:_Preprocessor._process_parse_type_triple, ns17:_Preprocessor.process ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/rdfxml12.py" ;
        slkg:isPrivate true ;
        slkg:lineEnd 330 ;
        slkg:lineStart 167 .

    ns17:_Preprocessor.__init__ dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.rdfxml12._Preprocessor.__init__" ;
        a slkg:Method ;
        rdfs:label "__init__" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/rdfxml12.py" ;
        slkg:isDunder true ;
        slkg:lineEnd 175 ;
        slkg:lineStart 173 ;
        slkg:signature "def __init__(self)" .

    ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.parsers.rdfxml12._Preprocessor._append_term_component" ;
        a slkg:Method ;
        rdfs:label "_append_term_component" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/parsers/rdfxml12.py" ;
        slkg:hasParameter ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component.param.node, ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component.param.local, ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component.param.parent ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component.returns ;
        slkg:isPrivate true ;
        slkg:lineEnd 250 ;
        slkg:lineStart 237 ;
        slkg:signature "def _append_term_component(self, parent: ET.Element, local: str, node) -> None" .

    ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component.param.local a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "local" ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str ;
        slkg:parameterKind "positional" ;
        slkg:position 1 .

    ns17:_Preprocessor._append_term_component.param.node a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "node" ;
