GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_resolve_imports.py> {
    ns111:test_resolve_imports.py dcterms:identifier "tests.graph.unit.test_resolve_imports" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """tests/unit/test_resolve_imports.py

Coverage for StarLayerGraph.owl_imports()/.resolve_imports() and the
standalone can_resolve_import() - generalizes validator.py's own
_resolve_shapes_graph_imports() (SHACL-specific, shacl_graph only) into a
plain graph capability any caller can use, with the same three-way mode=
contract infer() already established ("full"/"delta"/"in-place").

Retrieval policy is never this project's own decision - every test here
supplies its own explicit loader (a plain dict lookup), never a real
network call, matching the "no default loader" design: resolve_imports()
itself doesn't dictate how an IRI becomes a graph, only how to use the
result once a loader hands one back.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_resolve_imports" ;
        slkg:declares ns176:TestResolveImportsDeltaMode, ns176:TestCanResolveImport, ns176:TestOwlImports, ns176:TestResolveImportsFullMode, ns176:TestResolveImportsInPlaceMode, ns176:TestResolveImportsValidation, ns176:TestHasImportLocally, ns176:TestResolveImportsTransitiveClosure, ns176:TestResolveImportsSameGraphCoLocation ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/graph/unit/test_resolve_imports.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:rdflib, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:pytest .

