    ns245:test_nested_subject_triple_term_is_rejected dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.integration.test_adversarial_roundtrip.test_nested_subject_triple_term_is_rejected" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """A ground triple term used as *another* triple term's own subject is
invalid RDF 1.2 (see starlayer.sparql.triple_term.InvalidTripleTermError's
own docstring for the grammar citation and the full investigation this
module's own docstring references) - confirm it's rejected outright at
parse time, before any query ever reaches a backend. No live server
needed - this is pure parsing, unlike every other test in this file.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_nested_subject_triple_term_is_rejected" ;
        slkg:calls ns72:prepare_query_12 ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/integration/test_adversarial_roundtrip.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 440 ;
        slkg:lineStart 426 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_nested_subject_triple_term_is_rejected()" .

    ns245:test_pattern_subject_triple_term_is_rejected dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.integration.test_adversarial_roundtrip.test_pattern_subject_triple_term_is_rejected" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """The broader case (see module docstring): a triple term used as the
subject of an *ordinary* pattern - not nested inside another triple
term at all. `<<(:x ?R :z )>> :p <<(:a :b ?C )>> .` is the exact shape
the W3C `compound-tripleterm-subject` fixture's own first line uses
(`docs/w3c-sparql12-test-suite-issues.md` Issue 1) - confirmed to have
parsed and constructed without error before
`starlayer.sparql.triple_term._reject_triple_term_pattern_subjects` existed.
No live server needed - pure parsing.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_pattern_subject_triple_term_is_rejected" ;
        slkg:calls ns72:prepare_query_12 ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/integration/test_adversarial_roundtrip.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 459 ;
        slkg:lineStart 443 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_pattern_subject_triple_term_is_rejected()" .

    ns245:test_pattern_subject_triple_term_rejected_in_modify_where dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.integration.test_adversarial_roundtrip.test_pattern_subject_triple_term_rejected_in_modify_where" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Same broader rule, Update side: a Modify's WHERE clause is a nested
pattern tree reached only via generic recursion (not a top-level BGP a
naive, non-recursive check might special-case and stop at) - confirm
the walk actually reaches it. No live server needed - pure parsing.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_pattern_subject_triple_term_rejected_in_modify_where" ;
        slkg:calls ns72:prepare_update_12 ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/integration/test_adversarial_roundtrip.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 512 ;
