GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_source_rule_provenance.py> {
    ns97:test_source_rule_provenance.py dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_source_rule_provenance" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """``sh:sourceRule`` (SHACL 1.2 SPARQL Extensions section 8.7): opt-in
provenance tracking linking each rule-inferred triple back to the rule that
produced it, via a reifier (``_:id rdf:reifies <<( s p o )>> . _:id
sh:sourceRule <rule> .``). Off by default - the spec says a rule engine MAY
generate these triples, and they add nothing but noise to a caller who
didn't ask for them.

Covers both rule-execution paths this codebase has: shape-attached
``sh:rule``s (executed internally by pySHACL, intercepted via
``_patch_rule_apply_for_source_rule_provenance``) and standalone/global
``sh:SPARQLRule``s with no ``sh:rule`` edge (``_global_sparql_rule_triples``,
native starlayer.shacl code) - see ``tests/integration/test_global_sparql_rules.py``
for the base behavior these build on.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_source_rule_provenance" ;
        slkg:declares ns210:_source_rule_for, ns210:test_source_rule_provenance_covers_global_sparql_rules_too, ns210:test_source_rule_provenance_off_by_default_adds_nothing, ns210:test_source_rule_provenance_not_visible_to_executing_rules, ns210:test_source_rule_provenance_attributes_each_triple_to_its_own_rule, ns210:_two_rule_data, ns210:_two_rule_shapes ;
