GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/unit/test_query_collection.py> {
    ns120:test_query_collection.py dcterms:identifier "tests.sparql.unit.test_query_collection" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """``salg:QueryCollection`` — serializing a *set* of independent queries as
one RDF graph. The vocabulary (``salg:QueryCollection``/
``salg:queries``) already existed in ``salg-ontology.ttl``; this is the
first code that actually produces/consumes it.

Verifies the full loop the user asked for directly: take this project's own
existing test queries (``test_roundtrip.QUERIES``), encode them all as one
collection, round-trip through real Turtle *text* (not just an in-memory
Graph — the point of the feature is a ``.ttl`` file readable independently
of this project's own code), decode back, and confirm each decoded query
still *executes* to the same result as the original — the same
execution-based verification standard every other round-trip test in this
project uses, not a text- or structure-only comparison.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_query_collection" ;
        slkg:declares ns127:test_collection_roundtrips_through_turtle_text, ns127:test_collection_root_is_typed_and_distinct_from_member_queries, ns127:test_empty_collection_roundtrips ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/sparql/unit/test_query_collection.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:rdflib.plugins.sparql.processor, ns4:rdflib.plugins.sparql.evaluate, ns4:tests.sparql.unit.test_roundtrip, ns4:rdflib, ns4:rdflib.namespace .

