GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py> {
    ns97:test_sh_entailment.py dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_entailment" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py

End-to-end coverage for sh:entailment (SHACL 1.2 Core §1.4), via
StarShaclSchema.validate()/apply_rules() - see starlayer.shacl.entailment's
own module docstring for the spec citations this is built from.

Deliberately NOT testing plain rdfs:subClassOf-driven class membership
(e.g. a Dog/Canine example) - SHACL's own "SHACL type"/"SHACL instance"
definitions already give that unconditionally, with no sh:entailment
declaration needed at all (see test_subclass_reasoning_scope.py). These
tests instead use rdfs:domain, which genuinely needs an entailment regime
to take effect - a real, not vacuous, exercise of this feature.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_sh_entailment" ;
        slkg:declares ns206:TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput, ns206:TestTargetNodesRespectsEntailment, ns206:TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun, ns206:_shapes, ns206:_data, ns206:TestValidateRespectsShEntailment ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:rdflib, ns4:rdflib.namespace, ns4:pytest .

    ns206:TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_entailment.TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """apply_rules() gets "entailment before rules" for free, since
shape-attached sh:rule execution happens inside the same validate()
call that now applies sh:entailment first - see
starlayer/shacl/CLAUDE.md's own dated entry for the full design.

The entailed triple itself (ex:alice a ex:Employee) is never returned -
result.inferred_graph is strictly the rules' own output (the spec's
"inference graph"); entailment only needed to be visible to let the
rule *fire* in the first place.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun" ;
        slkg:declares ns206:TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun.test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 128 ;
        slkg:lineStart 94 .

    ns206:TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun.test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_entailment.TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun.test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires" ;
        a slkg:Method ;
        rdfs:label "test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires" ;
        slkg:calls ns206:_data ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py" ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns206:TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun.test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires.returns ;
        slkg:instantiates ns28:StarLayerGraph ;
        slkg:lineEnd 128 ;
        slkg:lineStart 105 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires(self) -> None" .

    ns206:TestApplyRulesSeesEntailmentBeforeRulesRun.test_rule_targeting_entailed_class_fires.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns206:TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_entailment.TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """The other gap this same session's design closes, independent of
sh:entailment: apply_rules()'s conforms/report_graph used to only ever
reflect the state BEFORE the global sh:SPARQLRule pass - triples that
pass produces were never actually validated at all. See
starlayer/shacl/CLAUDE.md's dated entry and the comment at
apply_rules()'s own final re-validation call site.""" ;
        rdfs:label "TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput" ;
        slkg:declares ns206:TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput.test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py" ;
        slkg:lineEnd 171 ;
        slkg:lineStart 131 .

    ns206:TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput.test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_entailment.TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput.test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output" ;
        a slkg:Method ;
        rdfs:label "test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_sh_entailment.py" ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns206:TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput.test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output.returns ;
        slkg:instantiates ns28:StarLayerGraph ;
        slkg:lineEnd 171 ;
        slkg:lineStart 139 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output(self) -> None" .

    ns206:TestApplyRulesValidatesGlobalRuleOutput.test_conforms_reflects_a_shape_violated_only_by_global_rule_output.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns206:TestTargetNodesRespectsEntailment dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_sh_entailment.TestTargetNodesRespectsEntailment" ;
        a slkg:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """2026-10-08: target_nodes() closed a consistency gap - it's now the
fifth processing function to see sh:entailment/inference=, matching
validate()/apply_rules()/evaluate()/extract_subgraph(). Same DATA/SHAPES
fixture as TestValidateRespectsShEntailment above: ex:worksAt
rdfs:domain ex:Employee genuinely needs an entailment regime to put
ex:alice in ex:EmployeeShape's own sh:targetClass membership - a
vacuous rdfs:subClassOf/"SHACL type" case wouldn't actually exercise
