GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_expected_predicate.py> {
    ns97:test_expected_predicate.py dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_expected_predicate" ;
        a slkg:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """sh:expectedPredicate (SHACL 1.2 SPARQL Extensions section 8.2.7,
"Expected Derived Triples") - both the sh:defaultValue and sh:values halves.

A rule declaring sh:expectedPredicate ex:p expects the *derived* triples for
ex:p - computed via sh:defaultValue/sh:values on every non-deactivated
property shape using ex:p as sh:path - to already be present before it
executes. sh:values here is SHACL 1.2 Core's *validation-time* computed-value
mechanism on an ordinary property shape (sh:select/sh:sparqlExpr/a node
expression - see _compute_sh_values in validator.py) - not the unrelated,
separately-tracked, genuinely unimplemented sh:PropertyRule/sh:values
shorthand (a sh:rule-construction mechanism, see that row in
docs/shacl12-gap-matrix.md's Core changelog table) that happens to share a
predicate name.

**Materialized triples are transient, not permanent** - confirmed 2026-08-15
via the W3C SHACL 1.2 test suite's own expectedPredicate-example fixture,
whose expected result includes only the dependent rule's own conclusions,
never the derived ex:area values themselves. An earlier version of this
feature (and this test file) assumed permanent materialization based on a
plausible but incorrect reading of the spec prose alone - corrected once
concrete fixture evidence was available.

starlayer.shacl/validator.py::_materialize_expected_predicates is the
implementation, hooked into the same always-applied
_patch_rules_apply_for_layer_and_run_once wrap item #3 (sh:layer/
sh:runOnce) already installs - see that function's own docstring for why
this lives there rather than as a third wrap of TripleRule.apply/
SPARQLRule.apply.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_expected_predicate" ;
        slkg:declares ns183:test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value, ns183:_rectangle_shapes, ns183:test_without_expected_predicate_default_value_is_never_materialized, ns183:test_shapes_graph_without_expected_predicate_uses_original_pyshacl_loop, ns183:test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs, ns183:test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_expected_predicate.py" ;
        slkg:importsModule ns4:rdflib, ns4:pytest .

    ns183:_rectangle_shapes dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_expected_predicate._rectangle_shapes" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:label "_rectangle_shapes" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_expected_predicate.py" ;
        slkg:hasParameter ns183:_rectangle_shapes.param.with_expected_predicate ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns183:_rectangle_shapes.returns ;
        slkg:isPrivate true ;
        slkg:lineEnd 63 ;
        slkg:lineStart 41 ;
        slkg:signature "def _rectangle_shapes(*, with_expected_predicate: bool) -> str" .

    ns183:_rectangle_shapes.param.with_expected_predicate a slkg:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "with_expected_predicate" ;
        slkg:annotationText "bool" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.bool ;
        slkg:parameterKind "kwonly" ;
        slkg:position 0 .

    ns183:_rectangle_shapes.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "str" ;
        slkg:hasType ns4:builtins.str .

    ns183:test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_expected_predicate.test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """ex:rect2 already asserts a real (large) ex:area - sh:defaultValue must
not be materialized on top of it, and the rule must see the real
asserted value, not the default.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value" ;
        slkg:calls ns183:_rectangle_shapes ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_expected_predicate.py" ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns183:test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value.returns ;
        slkg:instantiates ns28:StarLayerGraph ;
        slkg:lineEnd 120 ;
        slkg:lineStart 101 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value() -> None" .

    ns183:test_expected_predicate_does_not_override_an_existing_value.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns183:test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_expected_predicate.test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """No ex:area triple asserted anywhere - the rule's own WHERE clause can
only match if sh:expectedPredicate correctly materialized
ex:RectangleShape-area's sh:defaultValue (1) onto ex:rect1 first. The
materialized ex:area triple itself must NOT survive in the final output
though - transient, visible only during rule execution (see this file's
own module docstring for the concrete fixture evidence this is based
on) - only the rule's own conclusion (ex:isSmall) should persist.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs" ;
        slkg:calls ns183:_rectangle_shapes ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_expected_predicate.py" ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns183:test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs.returns ;
        slkg:instantiates ns28:StarLayerGraph ;
        slkg:lineEnd 83 ;
        slkg:lineStart 66 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs() -> None" .

    ns183:test_expected_predicate_materializes_default_value_before_rule_runs.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns183:test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_expected_predicate.test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """sh:values (sh:sparqlExpr form here) is consulted, and takes priority
over sh:defaultValue when it produces a result - both a real
sh:values-computed value distinct from the fallback default (a rule
depending on the *correct* value, not just "any" value, only fires
correctly if the real one was actually used) and the fallback-to-default
behavior for a focus node sh:values can't compute anything for are
exercised in one fixture, mirroring the SHACL 1.2 SPARQL Extensions
spec's own ex:RectangleShape-area worked example (sh:values computing a
real area via sparql:multiply/shnex:pathValues node expressions,
sh:defaultValue as the fallback) - covered end-to-end against the real
W3C fixture in tests/w3c_shacl12/ (sparql/rules/expectedPredicate-example),
this is the narrower unit-level check of the same priority logic.""" ;
        rdfs:label "test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value" ;
        slkg:filePath "packages/starlayer/tests/shacl/integration/test_expected_predicate.py" ;
        slkg:hasReturnValue ns183:test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value.returns ;
        slkg:instantiates ns28:StarLayerGraph ;
        slkg:lineEnd 207 ;
        slkg:lineStart 155 ;
        slkg:signature "def test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value() -> None" .

    ns183:test_expected_predicate_prefers_sh_values_over_default_value.returns a slkg:ReturnValue ;
        slkg:annotationText "None" ;
        slkg:optional true .

    ns183:test_shapes_graph_without_expected_predicate_uses_original_pyshacl_loop dcterms:identifier "tests.shacl.integration.test_expected_predicate.test_shapes_graph_without_expected_predicate_uses_original_pyshacl_loop" ;
        a slkg:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """A shapes graph with an ordinary sh:rule and no sh:expectedPredicate
anywhere sees zero behavior change - same fallback-safety bar as
